<title>VENEZUELA: Japan Ex-Im bank to loan Andean bank $100 mln.</title>
<headline>Japan Ex-Im bank to loan Andean bank $100 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Export-Import bank agreed Monday to lend the Andean Development Corporation (CAF) $100 million under an 11-year maturity non-binding loan, the CAF said.</p>
<p>The CAF, the financial arm of the Andean Community, said in a release it would use the loan to finance integration projects in member countries Bolivia, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and Venezuela.</p>
<p>The preliminary loan agreement signed by CAF President Enrique Garcia and Export-Import bank Governor Hiroshi Yasuda in Caracas will be sealed in Tokyo in November, the CAF said in a release.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
